# Incremental AMR / IntraLayout Studio work

This is an existing WinForms .NET 8 desktop app. Every task is an incremental update. Never rewrite working architecture unless Hakan explicitly asks.

## Scope

- Change only the files and blocks required for the requested task.
- Prefer small, surgical edits over refactors.
- Do not convert the app to WPF/MVVM unless asked. Use the existing WinForms path (caption hit-test / `SC_MOVE`, `CadToolTip`, `RibbonMenu`).

## Do not break

Do not alter, refactor, or remove these unless the task is specifically about them and there is no other way:

- Custom title bar and snap: `CaptionFrame.cs`, caption mouse handlers in `RibbonMenu` (`BeginNativeDrag`, `RestoreAndDrag`, drag-to-restore, double-click maximize)
- Global shortcuts: `CadShortcuts.cs`, `MainForm.ProcessCmdKey` (keep text-field exclusion)
- Working toolbars, buttons, and rich tooltips: `RibbonMenu.cs`, `CadToolTip.cs`

When touching shared chrome, preserve existing bindings and behavior. If a change could regress snap, shortcuts, or tips, leave those paths untouched.

## Assets

- Never load icons from Downloads or other machine-local paths.
- Put files in `Assets/Icons` or `Assets/Branding`.
- Keep them Embedded Resource / Content as in `DwgTrueView.App.csproj`.
- Load only through `AppIcons` (assembly + output copy).

## Approach

- Use the simplest framework-native option that already works here.
- Avoid new low-level Win32 unless the existing caption/snap path already requires it.
- When showing code to Hakan, give complete methods or files, not scattered fragments.
